ressure_held_for_mild_bleeds, test_pressure_falls_for_severe_bleeds"}], "visualizations": [{"name": "severity-response", "address": "local:HemorrhageSeverityResponse", "config": {"inputs_map": {"time": "global_time", "severity": "interventions.hemorrhage_severity", "mean_arterial_pressure": "vitals.mean_arterial_pressure_mmHg", "heart_rate": "vitals.heart_rate_bpm", "hemorrhaged_volume": "vitals.total_hemorrhaged_volume_mL"}}}], "robustness": {"n_replicates": 1, "parameter_sweep": true, "note": "Pulse is deterministic; the severity-0.8 pilot reproduced the earlier reference run to 4 significant figures."}, "controls": [{"name": "severity-0.0", "kind": "negative", "hypothesis": "With no bleed nothing is lost and the vitals stay at their loaded values.", "expected": "Less than 1 mL hemorrhaged; MAP and heart rate within 1 unit of their starting values.", "observed": "0 mL lost; MAP 95.3 -> 95.3 mmHg; heart rate 72.0 -> 71.2 /min.", "result": "PASS"}, {"name": "severity-1.0", "kind": "positive", "hypothesis": "A maximal bleed produces the largest, unambiguous loss and the deepest pressure fall, confirming the readout responds when the effect is certainly present.", "expected": "The largest hemorrhaged volume of the sweep and the lowest MAP.", "observed": "1793 mL lost (most of any arm); MAP 95.3 -> 78.1 mmHg (largest fall).", "result": "PASS"}], "preregistered": {"registered_at": "2026-10-23", "criteria": ["tests/test_severity.py::test_no_bleed_control_is_flat", "tests/test_severity.py::test_blood_loss_rises_with_severity", "tests/test_severity.py::test_heart_rate_rises_with_severity", "tests/test_severity.py::test_pressure_held_for_mild_bleeds", "tests/test_severity.py::test_pressure_falls_for_severe_bleeds", "tests/test_severity.py::test_reproduces_reference_run"], "predictions": ["Pilot probe (direct pulse_hemorrhage runs, 600 s): severity 0.2 / 0.5 / 0.8 lost 386 / 1040 / 1577 mL; heart rate 76 / 95 / 107 bpm; MAP 95.0 / 94.8 / 84.1 mmHg from 95.3."], "thresholds_provenance": "Thresholds come from that pilot probe and from the reference run in .build-progress.md (RightLeg 0.8, 600 s, BV 3936 mL, MAP 84.1 mmHg).", "pilot": "Criteria were written after a direct pilot (workspace/experiments/_runs.yaml, pilot-2026-10-23-severity) at severity 0.2, 0.5 and 0.8. Pulse is deterministic, so the criteria at 0.2 and 0.8 were set knowing those outcomes; severity 0.0, 0.4, 0.6 and 1.0 were not run before the canonical runs."}, "falsifiability": "The hypothesis is refuted if blood loss or heart rate fails to increase with\nseverity, if MAP drops more than 2 mmHg at severity 0.2 or 0.4, or if MAP at\nseverity 0.8 is not at least 8 mmHg below its starting value.\n", "limitations": ["One patient (StandardMale), one site (RightLeg) and 10 minutes; longer bleeds and other sites are not covered.", "Severity is Pulse's own dimensionless scale, not a calibrated flow rate.", "Acceptance bands trace to the deterministic pilot and the .build-progress.md reference run, not to external physiology literature (none was provided), so they are regression checks on Pulse's behaviour, not a validation against data."], "alternative_hypotheses": [{"hypothesis": "MAP is held at low severity only because less blood is lost, not by active compensation.", "status": "excluded", "evidence": "Blood loss rises monotonically with severity (F-01) while MAP is still held flat through severity 0.4; the pressure is maintained despite increasing loss, so reduced loss cannot be the explanation."}, {"hypothesis": "The heart-rate rise is incidental and does not defend pressure.", "status": "excluded", "evidence": "MAP stays within 1.1 mmHg of start exactly over the range where heart rate climbs and cardiac output is still near baseline, and breaks only once cardiac output falls (F-02, F-04); the tachycardia tracks the pressure defence."}, {"hypothesis": "The last-step deferral or the fixed 1 s record step distorts the severity-0.8 numbers.", "status": "excluded", "evidence": "